{
  "group": "verify",
  "upstream": "pbkdf2@3.1.6",
  "note": "Verifying a password against a KNOWN derived key - the flow a login performs. Every correct key here was produced by the upstream oracle; the port reaches it through its own encoded form (pbkdf2_<alg>$iterations$b64salt$b64dk), so pwhash.Decode and pwhash.Verify are both under test. The rejection corpus covers wrong passwords, substituted salts, iteration counts and algorithms, and tampered, truncated, lengthened, empty and non-hex stored keys.",
